WEBVTT

00:17.225 --> 00:18.143
Huh?

00:46.629 --> 00:48.131
It's a monitor.

02:47.375 --> 02:48.793
This is CGI, right?

02:49.294 --> 02:50.336
"CGI"?

02:50.962 --> 02:52.088
Really?

03:42.889 --> 03:44.349
- Missed you.
- Same here.

03:44.933 --> 03:46.684
- I picked this up.
- Thanks.

03:47.560 --> 03:49.562
I'm so hungry.

04:44.200 --> 04:45.285
Usagi?

04:48.037 --> 04:49.038
Arisu.

05:01.968 --> 05:03.136
At last,

05:04.595 --> 05:05.763
I found you.

05:08.474 --> 05:09.475
I'm sorry.

05:18.526 --> 05:19.694
Let's go home.

05:23.531 --> 05:24.365
Yeah.

05:25.700 --> 05:26.909
Ouch.

05:27.994 --> 05:28.911
Sorry.

06:09.702 --> 06:10.870
You…

06:11.662 --> 06:13.081
- Hey!
- Ryuji!

06:13.164 --> 06:16.501
Why are you with Usagi?
She's dead because of you!

06:16.584 --> 06:17.877
You son of a bitch!

06:17.960 --> 06:19.170
Stop, Arisu!

06:19.253 --> 06:20.213
- Arisu!
- Ryuji?

06:20.296 --> 06:22.215
Ryuji, are you all right?

06:22.298 --> 06:24.509
Okay, there you go.

06:27.303 --> 06:30.515
- He's been fighting alongside me.
- Usagi…

06:30.598 --> 06:33.810
I made it this far, thanks to him.

06:34.811 --> 06:37.063
- Still--
- He saved my life.

06:38.356 --> 06:40.358
I'm with you now, thanks to him.

06:51.119 --> 06:53.162
Entry is now closed.

06:54.914 --> 06:57.250
There are ten players.

06:58.334 --> 07:00.044
"Ten players"?

07:01.170 --> 07:03.131
There are only nine here.

07:03.881 --> 07:05.133
I don't get it.

07:06.759 --> 07:07.760
A child.

07:08.344 --> 07:09.262
What?

07:12.181 --> 07:13.266
There's a child.

07:20.148 --> 07:22.358
You're pregnant, Usagi.

07:25.987 --> 07:28.614
We're having a baby?

07:30.616 --> 07:32.034
Yes, a baby.

07:36.539 --> 07:37.540
I get it.

07:38.291 --> 07:40.918
The baby in her belly makes it ten.

07:41.502 --> 07:43.212
Congrats!

07:43.296 --> 07:47.049
But a child in this situation is…

07:55.850 --> 07:57.560
The game will now commence.

07:58.352 --> 07:59.604
It's starting.

08:00.188 --> 08:03.149
Please put on the wristbands and collars.

08:18.122 --> 08:20.708
The game is Future Sugoroku.

09:50.006 --> 09:51.132
Here are the rules.

09:53.926 --> 09:59.932
There are a total of 25 rooms
arranged in five rows and five columns.

10:01.267 --> 10:05.521
Roll the dice on the platform
in the center of each room.

10:05.605 --> 10:09.859
The numbers you roll determine
how many people can advance to each room.

10:11.027 --> 10:16.073
Repeat this as you try to reach
the exit room within 15 turns.

10:16.157 --> 10:18.409
EXIT

10:20.828 --> 10:24.540
However, if there are more people
than the numbers rolled,

10:24.624 --> 10:27.960
the excess individuals
cannot leave the room.

10:28.628 --> 10:31.464
The doors will be locked,
forcing them to stay.

10:31.547 --> 10:33.507
FORCED STAY

10:34.759 --> 10:38.137
To unlock the room,
use the transceiver on the wristband

10:38.220 --> 10:43.142
to coordinate and position players
on opposite sides of the locked room.

10:43.225 --> 10:46.520
UNLOCKED

10:47.188 --> 10:50.483
You have each been allocated 15 points.

10:53.819 --> 10:55.488
To pass through a door,

10:55.571 --> 11:01.369
one of you must use one point
by holding your wristband up to it.

11:04.080 --> 11:08.417
To return to the previous room,
you must stay where you are for one turn.

11:08.501 --> 11:11.504
The door will only be unlocked after that.

11:12.713 --> 11:16.842
Whether you choose to
or are forced to stay,

11:16.926 --> 11:20.054
one point will be used each turn.

11:20.971 --> 11:23.683
It's game over if you run out of points.

11:28.437 --> 11:34.944
The walls through which you can proceed
will display images of your future.

11:35.027 --> 11:37.947
The one that you choose

11:38.030 --> 11:43.119
is the future
that will come to pass once you exit.

11:46.914 --> 11:49.125
"The future that will come to pass."

11:51.544 --> 11:56.632
THE FUTURE THAT WILL COME TO PASS

11:57.508 --> 12:00.219
Proceed according to the dice rolls

12:00.302 --> 12:04.598
and choose your future
as you search for the exit.

12:05.766 --> 12:09.145
So we need to work together
to find the exit?

12:14.400 --> 12:15.985
May I ask your names?

12:21.699 --> 12:23.909
I'm Sohta, and this is my sister--

12:23.993 --> 12:24.994
I'm Yuna.

12:25.828 --> 12:26.912
I'm Arisu.

12:28.789 --> 12:34.628
This is Sachiko, Rei, Tetsu, and Nobu.

12:36.922 --> 12:41.635
Now roll the dice,
and then choose which room to enter.

12:42.303 --> 12:44.138
You have three minutes.

13:01.155 --> 13:04.033
So the dice colors
correspond to the doors.

13:05.075 --> 13:06.076
Okay!

13:06.786 --> 13:08.662
Dice are my specialty.

13:09.288 --> 13:11.248
Because you're a gambling addict?

13:12.958 --> 13:15.419
First turn. Begin.

13:21.008 --> 13:22.092
Okay.

13:52.998 --> 13:55.084
Is this really the future?

13:57.086 --> 13:59.463
Is this for real?

14:07.805 --> 14:10.641
- Here it comes!
- You won again?

14:10.724 --> 14:13.644
Bonus mode!

14:16.355 --> 14:18.107
We give thanks for this meal.

14:18.190 --> 14:19.483
What?

14:19.567 --> 14:20.860
Really?

14:25.531 --> 14:29.118
The future is different on each wall.

14:29.618 --> 14:31.161
Goddamn machine!

14:35.165 --> 14:36.125
Shit!

14:39.336 --> 14:42.673
Your future changes depending on the door?

14:49.638 --> 14:50.556
Please.

14:52.266 --> 14:55.644
Matsuyama, it's time
to study something else.

14:55.728 --> 14:59.064
Please, just a glance.
Please read it, Professor.

14:59.148 --> 15:01.317
It'll all be for nothing if I quit now.

15:08.365 --> 15:12.328
The Academy isn't going to
waste their time reading this nonsense.

15:13.746 --> 15:15.539
Please read it, at least.

15:16.832 --> 15:19.752
You should submit that
to occult magazines.

15:37.770 --> 15:39.730
Okay, smile.

15:39.813 --> 15:40.814
Smile.

15:42.858 --> 15:43.817
Nice day, huh?

15:44.401 --> 15:46.111
Yeah, feels great.

15:47.237 --> 15:49.406
If I have my choice of futures,

15:50.074 --> 15:51.825
I'll pick the blue door.

15:53.160 --> 15:54.328
Me too.

15:55.287 --> 15:58.832
But only seven people
can go through the blue door.

16:00.042 --> 16:01.877
One person for the yellow door?

16:04.546 --> 16:06.507
- All right!
- Nice shot, Hida!

16:06.590 --> 16:07.925
Nice!

16:08.842 --> 16:10.719
I prefer yellow.

16:12.179 --> 16:17.977
No, the key to this game is minimizing
point loss as we make our way through.

16:18.560 --> 16:21.855
So we should move together
whenever possible.

16:23.899 --> 16:29.196
We should split into two groups
of the largest numbers, seven and five.

16:30.447 --> 16:34.702
Sohta and Yuna,
would you go to room D3 with Rei?

16:36.870 --> 16:37.705
You three…

16:40.666 --> 16:43.210
will go to the room to the east, D3.

16:43.877 --> 16:46.296
We'll go to the room to the north, C2.

16:46.839 --> 16:50.843
Based on the diagram,
we can quickly regroup in D2.

16:51.552 --> 16:52.886
D3.

16:54.388 --> 16:56.682
- Do it.
- Yuna.

16:56.765 --> 16:59.852
Ken? I didn't notice you were here!

16:59.935 --> 17:00.936
This is my brother.

17:01.020 --> 17:02.813
Ken is a college classmate…

17:02.896 --> 17:03.939
Understood.

17:05.149 --> 17:07.151
We're fine with the red door.

17:08.318 --> 17:10.654
One minute remaining.

17:12.740 --> 17:14.950
- Then, it's decided.
- Let's go.

17:15.034 --> 17:17.369
Why do you trust him?

17:20.205 --> 17:22.624
You're free to choose another door.

17:34.803 --> 17:40.809
Hold your wristband to the chosen door
and proceed to the next room.

17:44.563 --> 17:45.939
All right, let's go.

18:00.079 --> 18:01.371
We'll regroup later.

18:01.455 --> 18:02.664
Okay.

18:17.262 --> 18:18.764
I'm Rei Morikage.

18:18.847 --> 18:22.142
I've loved anime since I was a kid.

18:22.226 --> 18:23.769
I draw a lot.

18:24.394 --> 18:26.647
How quickly do you draw?

18:27.147 --> 18:31.401
It currently takes me three days
to complete one drawing…

18:34.488 --> 18:38.408
C2 is a minus-one-point room.

18:38.909 --> 18:43.330
- Please select whose points to use.
- Why is it deducting a point?

18:43.831 --> 18:47.126
Some rooms probably have a point penalty.

18:47.751 --> 18:51.588
We won't know till we enter,
which makes it tricky.

18:53.006 --> 18:56.969
We just used Arisu's points,
so let's use mine.

19:03.183 --> 19:05.477
Second turn. Begin.

19:14.153 --> 19:19.032
Now roll the dice,
and then choose which room to enter.

19:20.701 --> 19:23.370
We can't return to the last room
without waiting a turn.

19:23.453 --> 19:26.665
That leaves three rooms,
which explains the three dice.

19:27.166 --> 19:28.917
All right!

19:36.008 --> 19:38.177
Three, one, five?

19:51.565 --> 19:54.026
If this really is the future,

19:54.610 --> 19:57.529
I'd choose the blue door in this room too.

19:57.613 --> 19:59.281
MOVIE TICKET
EVERYBODY LOVES FAMILY!

19:59.781 --> 20:02.993
- We should do this now and then.
- I wanted to see this.

20:06.538 --> 20:08.498
CLASS 1 ARCHITECT
DESIGN DRAWING EXAM

20:10.584 --> 20:11.460
What?

20:11.960 --> 20:14.755
You're gonna try to be an architect?

20:17.633 --> 20:18.592
I am?

20:21.470 --> 20:24.556
What would you do
if a student were bullied in your class?

20:24.640 --> 20:26.391
Mr. Hida, what do you think?

20:26.475 --> 20:30.270
- I wouldn't just stop it.
- The future that will come to pass.

20:30.354 --> 20:31.939
I'd first listen to both…

20:32.022 --> 20:34.191
I don't wanna choose the red door.

20:42.115 --> 20:45.702
Hida, there's an interesting seminar.
Wanna go?

20:45.786 --> 20:47.246
SKILL DEVELOPMENT SEMINAR

20:47.329 --> 20:48.997
I don't have time.

20:49.081 --> 20:52.292
Think of it as an investment
in your future self.

20:52.376 --> 20:54.753
At least go hear what they have to say.

20:56.672 --> 20:58.340
Please sign your name here.

20:58.924 --> 21:00.884
Okay, thank you.

21:00.968 --> 21:03.178
- Please take a seat.
- All right.

21:03.262 --> 21:07.182
D2 is beyond the red door.
That's where we plan to regroup.

21:07.975 --> 21:13.063
I'll go through the red door to the east
and meet up with Rei and the others.

21:13.814 --> 21:14.898
I'll go too.

21:16.858 --> 21:21.446
Can I ask the rest of you
to go through the blue door to room C1?

21:21.530 --> 21:25.450
You did it, Matsuyama.
It's the research funding you wanted.

21:25.534 --> 21:28.245
- Is this for real?
- Yes, congratulations.

21:28.829 --> 21:30.163
Thank you very much.

21:32.874 --> 21:34.084
Let's meet up later.

21:41.174 --> 21:42.175
All right.

21:43.760 --> 21:44.594
Let's go.

21:52.227 --> 21:54.771
TO: YUZUHA ARISU

21:54.855 --> 21:57.858
THANK YOU FOR THE OTHER DAY
CAN WE MEET?

22:02.821 --> 22:05.157
This is getting weird.

22:06.742 --> 22:10.370
Is this game peeking into our minds?

22:21.089 --> 22:21.923
All twos.

22:35.437 --> 22:37.856
I'll head north to D2.

22:38.398 --> 22:43.528
I wish the three of us could go together,
but we have to split into two groups.

22:44.946 --> 22:45.947
Got it.

22:47.115 --> 22:50.786
We'll go east to E3.

22:51.286 --> 22:52.120
Okay.

22:52.704 --> 22:54.581
JOB OFFER CONFIRMATION

22:55.791 --> 22:57.042
No way!

23:01.922 --> 23:03.465
This is delicious!

23:03.548 --> 23:05.258
Hey, are you listening to me?

23:11.098 --> 23:14.684
Rei, let's meet up in room D2 as planned.

23:15.352 --> 23:16.353
Roger that.

23:27.739 --> 23:29.616
- Okay.
- Thank goodness.

23:29.699 --> 23:30.534
Yeah.

23:31.034 --> 23:33.495
Third turn. Begin.

23:35.789 --> 23:37.749
Huh? One and two?

23:49.886 --> 23:54.057
Usagi counts as two,
so she can only go to D1.

23:54.975 --> 23:57.185
Only one can go to E2.

23:57.686 --> 24:00.730
So one of us will be forced to stay.

24:03.442 --> 24:07.154
Everyone, this is Morikage.
She'll be starting today.

24:07.654 --> 24:09.948
I look forward to working with you.

24:10.031 --> 24:11.074
I'm Rei Morikage.

24:11.158 --> 24:12.993
It's nice to meet you.

24:14.995 --> 24:16.830
I guess it can't be helped.

24:19.749 --> 24:21.543
I'll stay this time.

24:21.626 --> 24:22.794
What?

24:23.503 --> 24:25.088
Keep your kid safe.

24:25.755 --> 24:27.507
- But…
- Rei.

24:28.216 --> 24:30.469
I owe you one from Zombie Hunt.

24:39.895 --> 24:42.522
Meet up with Sachiko and the others.

24:45.108 --> 24:46.568
Sachiko, are you there?

24:52.240 --> 24:53.575
Yeah, I can hear you.

24:54.701 --> 24:56.578
How many can go to D1?

24:58.622 --> 25:00.332
Four. We all can.

25:01.791 --> 25:02.834
That's great.

25:03.335 --> 25:07.422
- Then please head east to D1.
- I'm sick of your nagging.

25:07.506 --> 25:09.799
- Meet with Usagi there.
- Let's not fight here.

25:09.883 --> 25:12.219
This place isn't good enough for you?

25:12.302 --> 25:15.180
- That's not what I meant.
- Did I ask you to apologize?

25:16.348 --> 25:17.307
Roger that.

25:19.351 --> 25:23.230
Sohta and Yuna,
could you please stay where you are?

25:24.356 --> 25:28.151
Usagi and I will move this turn,
and Rei will be forced to stay.

25:29.319 --> 25:32.155
I want you to return to D3 after one turn.

25:32.781 --> 25:35.617
That will end Rei's forced stay.

25:36.451 --> 25:38.703
After that, let's meet at E3.

25:39.579 --> 25:41.289
It's best to stay together.

25:41.373 --> 25:43.375
So we should stay. Understood.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.842
All right, let's all go to D1.

25:53.343 --> 25:56.471
Because Arisu said
to move together whenever possible?

25:57.889 --> 26:01.685
- I mean--
- Listen, we need to find the exit.

26:02.269 --> 26:05.021
We might find it faster if we split up.

26:06.314 --> 26:07.607
Besides,

26:09.067 --> 26:11.653
shouldn't we give our futures
a little more thought?

26:30.880 --> 26:31.965
Mr. Matsuyama!

26:32.924 --> 26:34.384
Look at these numbers.

26:34.467 --> 26:38.138
I think these results are enough
to prove your hypothesis.

26:38.221 --> 26:40.473
You did it! This is amazing!

26:41.975 --> 26:46.521
You'll go out there and sell this water
for 3,000 yen per bottle.

26:47.188 --> 26:50.066
You're free to leave now if you want out.

26:50.150 --> 26:53.778
If you're serious about
changing your life, come with me.

26:53.862 --> 26:56.364
Why did you join this seminar?

26:56.448 --> 26:58.700
To awaken my true potential.

26:58.783 --> 27:00.535
That's right.

27:00.619 --> 27:04.998
This time, you're going to sell this water
for 30,000 yen per bottle.

27:06.458 --> 27:09.127
Do you understand why you have to sell it?

27:09.210 --> 27:10.629
TRUE AWAKENING
LUCKY WATER

27:10.712 --> 27:13.131
- Excuse me…
- No thanks.

27:14.090 --> 27:15.967
No, thank you.

27:16.051 --> 27:17.260
This is impossible.

27:17.344 --> 27:19.596
- Please let me return them.
- Cut the crap!

27:19.679 --> 27:22.015
It's in the contract you signed.

27:22.098 --> 27:24.309
No returns allowed!

27:26.311 --> 27:27.604
- I'm sorry.
- Huh?!

27:27.687 --> 27:29.939
He's so drunk. I'm so sorry!

27:30.023 --> 27:32.275
What do you mean, you're sorry?

27:33.068 --> 27:35.654
- Why are you apologizing?
- Stop it!

27:35.737 --> 27:36.738
Please, just…

27:36.821 --> 27:38.615
REJECTION LETTER

27:42.994 --> 27:44.245
You're hired.

27:44.329 --> 27:45.246
Really?

27:45.747 --> 27:47.582
We look forward to working with you.

27:48.166 --> 27:49.292
Thank you very much.

27:49.376 --> 27:52.003
- Thanks for coming.
- Thank you for hiring me.

27:58.093 --> 28:00.845
The exit is likely
in one of the corner rooms,

28:00.929 --> 28:03.348
as they are the furthest from the center.

28:05.517 --> 28:08.395
It might be worth a shot.

28:10.105 --> 28:10.939
Yeah.

28:12.565 --> 28:15.985
So let's split into two groups
and head for the corner rooms.

28:16.569 --> 28:19.823
But I don't want to ignore
what Arisu said.

28:19.906 --> 28:23.660
So how about the two of us
go this way as a compromise?

28:24.369 --> 28:29.165
I'll meet up with Usagi,
and you'll go towards the corner room.

28:30.834 --> 28:31.751
Fine.

28:33.712 --> 28:34.921
Okay, then.

28:36.256 --> 28:37.382
We'll go to B1.

28:38.341 --> 28:39.300
That okay?

28:40.677 --> 28:41.803
I guess.

28:57.819 --> 28:58.820
Let's break up.

29:00.238 --> 29:01.406
I don't love you anymore.

29:02.157 --> 29:04.033
Did I do something wrong?

29:04.117 --> 29:05.410
Look, Sohta.

29:06.119 --> 29:06.953
I'm sorry.

29:07.454 --> 29:09.622
No, wait, Ken! Don't go!

29:11.207 --> 29:12.208
Why?

29:13.251 --> 29:15.962
We're going to get married.

29:17.046 --> 29:18.506
Please give us your blessing.

29:20.049 --> 29:21.050
Is that right?

29:21.885 --> 29:23.386
- Yeah.
- Congratulations.

29:23.470 --> 29:25.221
- Thanks.
- Thank you very much.

29:51.998 --> 29:54.417
Wow! Look at that huge lake.

29:54.501 --> 29:56.711
No, Yuna. It's a dam.

29:56.795 --> 29:57.754
What? A dam?

29:57.837 --> 30:00.381
- It's a lake formed by a dam.
- Like a reservoir?

30:00.965 --> 30:02.550
Then she's half right!

30:02.634 --> 30:04.844
See? I'm half right.

30:04.928 --> 30:06.805
Yuna, you're so excited today.

30:06.888 --> 30:10.350
Of course! It's been so long
since we went out as a family.

30:10.433 --> 30:12.268
- It's so fun!
- That's right.

30:29.077 --> 30:30.954
We did everything we could,

30:32.747 --> 30:36.042
but I'm afraid
your parents didn't make it.

31:50.783 --> 31:56.581
Hold your wristband to the chosen door
and proceed to the next room.

32:03.379 --> 32:04.380
Sohta,

32:05.298 --> 32:06.132
are you sure?

32:23.524 --> 32:24.984
Forced stay.

32:27.862 --> 32:29.572
You're completely useless!

32:34.994 --> 32:35.828
What?

32:38.790 --> 32:40.583
You're completely useless!

32:42.043 --> 32:43.169
What is this?!

32:45.046 --> 32:46.381
1 ROOM

32:46.464 --> 32:48.508
Point deduction confirmed.

32:49.425 --> 32:51.761
Fourth turn. Begin.

32:52.887 --> 32:54.681
- I'll roll the dice
- Okay.

33:20.289 --> 33:22.709
Yellow to the west is a corner room.

33:23.459 --> 33:24.836
But only one of us can go.

33:26.879 --> 33:28.881
It's better not to split up now.

33:30.383 --> 33:31.634
Let's go south to B2.

33:32.135 --> 33:34.929
You did it. You got a job offer!

33:35.013 --> 33:37.598
- A job offer, Nobu? Congrats.
- Congrats.

33:37.682 --> 33:38.516
Well done!

33:38.599 --> 33:39.434
Nobu!

33:41.602 --> 33:42.603
You listening?

33:43.563 --> 33:46.315
- Yeah.
- You did it. You got a job offer!

33:46.399 --> 33:49.569
You got a job offer, Nobu? Congrats.

33:49.652 --> 33:52.572
Let's stay here so we can get Rei out.

33:54.490 --> 33:56.743
I'll check the corner room next door.

33:56.826 --> 33:58.369
What if it's a trap?

33:58.453 --> 34:00.079
I still have 15 points.

34:00.163 --> 34:01.164
I'll be fine.

34:05.251 --> 34:06.252
Sohta,

34:07.086 --> 34:08.838
what numbers did you roll?

34:15.845 --> 34:16.846
Sohta.

34:18.306 --> 34:20.767
Sohta? Yuna?

34:21.768 --> 34:23.770
You're currently staying at E3, right?

34:24.520 --> 34:27.774
Can you move to D3? Please unlock Rei.

34:29.108 --> 34:30.151
Understood.

34:31.736 --> 34:32.653
Are you sure?

34:35.656 --> 34:36.491
Look.

34:42.997 --> 34:45.166
A corner room is behind the green door.

34:46.250 --> 34:47.960
The exit might be there.

34:48.586 --> 34:50.296
Arisu wouldn't try to save us

34:50.838 --> 34:55.134
if it meant losing
Usagi and his unborn child.

34:59.138 --> 35:00.973
For Mom and Dad's sake,

35:01.808 --> 35:04.060
we need to head toward that future.

35:15.238 --> 35:16.280
Let's go.

35:17.365 --> 35:18.199
Okay.

35:22.787 --> 35:23.788
I'll do it.

35:31.003 --> 35:33.422
Rei, are you okay?

35:33.506 --> 35:36.050
Hurry! I feel like I'm going insane!

35:36.926 --> 35:39.095
Sohta and Yuna are heading to D3.

35:39.178 --> 35:40.888
You should be unlocked soon.

35:43.808 --> 35:45.143
Please!

36:04.370 --> 36:05.997
- Congrats!
- Congrats!

36:07.373 --> 36:08.207
Hey!

36:09.625 --> 36:10.751
Let's go.

36:12.920 --> 36:14.589
I'll use my points.

37:03.512 --> 37:06.098
He sells weird water. It's Nobu!

37:07.558 --> 37:10.561
Drink up, and I'll buy a bottle. Go on!

37:10.645 --> 37:16.067
- Chug it!
- Chug it!

37:16.150 --> 37:17.151
Go on, chug it!

37:19.111 --> 37:20.529
Next one!

37:21.155 --> 37:23.574
- Next one!
- Chug it!

37:23.658 --> 37:27.078
- Why do you have that?
- Hey!

37:27.161 --> 37:29.747
- I have it 'cause I wanna drink!
- Hey!

37:29.830 --> 37:32.541
Drink!

37:32.625 --> 37:34.335
Chug!

37:34.418 --> 37:36.462
I can't drink anymore. I give up.

37:36.963 --> 37:38.756
Got something to say?

37:38.839 --> 37:43.177
Say it after drinking!

37:43.261 --> 37:44.720
- Okay!
- Chug!

37:44.804 --> 37:49.600
Say it after drinking!

37:49.684 --> 37:50.559
Chug!

37:50.643 --> 37:51.978
Say it after drinking!

37:53.729 --> 37:55.690
- Disgusting!
- That's so gross!

37:55.773 --> 37:56.774
I'm sorry.

37:56.857 --> 37:58.901
Seriously, drop dead!

38:00.945 --> 38:05.241
Drop dead!

38:07.118 --> 38:09.620
Tetsu, I'm sorry.

38:10.579 --> 38:11.414
Hey!

38:14.000 --> 38:15.001
Nobu!

38:15.918 --> 38:18.129
What the hell is he doing?

38:30.808 --> 38:32.643
I'm all alone now.

38:33.394 --> 38:34.603
- 6 ROOM
NOBUAKI HIDA: 13

38:34.687 --> 38:38.649
A1 is a minus-six-point room.

38:38.733 --> 38:39.775
Seriously?

38:45.197 --> 38:46.782
It wasn't the exit room.

38:47.283 --> 38:50.119
And it's a corner room,
so there's only one door.

38:51.912 --> 38:55.041
E5 is a minus-four-point room.

38:55.124 --> 38:55.958
What?

38:57.668 --> 38:59.503
- 4 ROOM
SOHTA ITSUKI: 13, YUNA ITSUKI: 14

38:59.587 --> 39:00.671
Damn it.

39:02.006 --> 39:03.090
We'll use mine.

39:03.174 --> 39:04.133
But…

39:05.801 --> 39:07.970
Point deduction confirmed.

39:11.057 --> 39:11.932
It's okay.

39:13.934 --> 39:16.604
Fifth turn. Begin.

39:21.567 --> 39:23.736
Rei, did you get out?

39:24.737 --> 39:28.949
I'm still stuck here.
And I lost another point!

39:29.033 --> 39:29.950
What?

39:35.373 --> 39:37.249
- Come on in.
- Thank you.

39:37.875 --> 39:40.628
- Here, Yuna.
- You shouldn't have.

39:40.711 --> 39:43.172
Sohta, Yuna. Where are you?

39:43.255 --> 39:44.590
You have great taste.

39:46.550 --> 39:48.344
This is far from finished.

39:48.427 --> 39:50.304
Sohta! Yuna!

39:52.390 --> 39:53.557
Sohta! Yuna!

40:01.482 --> 40:03.317
This is far from finished.

40:04.360 --> 40:10.116
When push comes to shove,
people choose the future they want

40:11.617 --> 40:15.538
instead of helping others.

40:21.085 --> 40:23.087
FROM: MOM
PLEASE JUST CALL ONCE

40:27.967 --> 40:29.718
This is far from finished.

40:30.302 --> 40:32.179
You're completely useless.

40:32.263 --> 40:37.268
Come to think of it,
I wonder how Mom is doing.

40:41.939 --> 40:42.982
Shit.

40:48.487 --> 40:49.780
Gimme one packet.

40:49.864 --> 40:52.450
That stuff rocked, right?

41:15.181 --> 41:16.348
No way in hell.

41:18.726 --> 41:20.978
Didn't I just toss the drugs?

41:27.443 --> 41:28.360
No!

41:29.737 --> 41:31.655
Shit! No!

41:32.907 --> 41:33.991
No!

41:46.462 --> 41:47.505
Mom.

41:49.048 --> 41:51.675
Your mother had
a severe cerebral hemorrhage.

41:51.759 --> 41:52.843
No way.

41:54.011 --> 41:55.012
Nobu…

41:57.640 --> 42:01.352
Even if she recovers,
I doubt she'll return to the life she had.

42:01.435 --> 42:02.937
This can't be true.

42:15.699 --> 42:16.534
Usagi.

42:17.284 --> 42:21.705
I'll go unlock Rei in D3,
so stay there again the next turn.

42:22.456 --> 42:23.332
Got it.

42:24.500 --> 42:25.501
Ryuji.

42:26.210 --> 42:29.004
Ryuji, can you hear me?
How are things there?

42:30.256 --> 42:32.925
Corner room E1 deducts one point.

42:33.676 --> 42:34.802
So no exit?

42:35.386 --> 42:36.387
Nope.

42:52.486 --> 42:53.487
No.

42:55.114 --> 42:56.115
It can't be.

43:05.583 --> 43:06.584
No.

43:08.919 --> 43:09.920
This can't be.

43:13.382 --> 43:14.383
I'm screwed.

43:19.054 --> 43:20.139
Mom.

43:22.641 --> 43:24.059
It's my fault.

43:29.815 --> 43:30.983
It's all my fault.

44:07.895 --> 44:09.897
This is far from finished.

44:11.231 --> 44:12.483
D2 UNLOCKED

44:17.071 --> 44:20.366
Room D2 has been unlocked.

44:23.702 --> 44:25.871
Rei, you should be able to move now.

44:27.706 --> 44:29.124
See you next turn.

44:31.585 --> 44:32.586
Roger that.

44:33.879 --> 44:34.838
Thanks.

44:54.024 --> 44:55.359
- 4 ROOM
TETSU SHIMAZAKI: 12

44:55.442 --> 44:58.737
B3 is a minus-four-point room.

44:59.530 --> 45:01.532
Minus four?

45:03.409 --> 45:05.619
Point deduction confirmed.

45:12.084 --> 45:13.961
Tetsu? Nobu?

45:15.963 --> 45:17.798
Nobu! Answer me.

45:21.635 --> 45:25.222
There's nothing to worry about.
I still have points.

45:28.058 --> 45:30.227
Point deduction confirmed.

45:42.698 --> 45:43.741
Shit.

45:46.285 --> 45:47.578
Goddammit!

45:52.082 --> 45:53.751
Sorry I'm late.

45:58.172 --> 45:59.173
No worries.

46:02.718 --> 46:03.719
Yukiko.

46:10.434 --> 46:11.435
Hey, Yukiko.

46:11.518 --> 46:12.519
Yeah?

46:13.020 --> 46:15.272
How about the aquarium
for our anniversary?

46:15.939 --> 46:16.940
Why?

46:19.610 --> 46:20.986
I've never been.

46:21.069 --> 46:23.030
Never in your entire life?

46:23.530 --> 46:24.448
Yeah.

46:27.159 --> 46:28.076
Sure.

46:31.955 --> 46:34.291
Long time no see. You look well.

47:07.991 --> 47:09.660
Wow, look at you now.

47:11.578 --> 47:14.373
I'm working at an architectural firm.

47:14.915 --> 47:16.041
I can change.

47:16.542 --> 47:18.669
What? Really?

47:20.546 --> 47:22.464
I can change, Yukiko.

47:44.069 --> 47:45.320
Goddammit!

48:04.256 --> 48:05.799
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

48:06.300 --> 48:07.384
Welcome.

48:14.099 --> 48:15.434
I've been waiting.

48:15.517 --> 48:16.935
Sorry I'm late.

48:17.019 --> 48:18.812
I didn't think you'd come.

48:18.896 --> 48:21.356
What? Why wouldn't I?

48:23.233 --> 48:24.693
- Hey.
- What?

48:25.694 --> 48:28.155
- Want me to build you a house?
- Really?

48:28.238 --> 48:30.282
Yeah, what kind do you want?

48:31.742 --> 48:34.828
Big and spacious.

50:34.489 --> 50:38.035
A3 is a minus-eight-point room.

50:43.040 --> 50:45.584
You now have zero points.

50:47.544 --> 50:48.879
Game over.

50:54.426 --> 50:55.510
And there it is.

51:01.349 --> 51:03.518
Police. We have a search warrant.

51:06.813 --> 51:07.898
I found it!

51:17.908 --> 51:19.201
What's going on?

51:19.284 --> 51:21.870
- It's nothing.
- You haven't changed at all!

51:21.953 --> 51:23.455
Shut your mouth!

51:24.039 --> 51:27.042
What about you? I thought you trusted me!

51:27.125 --> 51:29.169
I did trust you!

51:29.795 --> 51:31.171
I trusted you.

51:31.671 --> 51:33.465
That's why it hurts even more!

51:40.347 --> 51:42.766
I guess this is goodbye.

52:04.371 --> 52:06.248
This seems about right.

52:20.679 --> 52:22.305
It's my fault.

52:42.325 --> 52:43.243
Nobu.

52:50.542 --> 52:52.294
Tell me what happened.

52:55.213 --> 52:56.631
Talk to me.

52:58.717 --> 52:59.676
Leave me alone.

53:01.595 --> 53:04.806
Tell me. I'm on your side.

53:22.574 --> 53:25.410
Whatever happens, I want you to live.

54:03.323 --> 54:04.324
Mom.

54:06.993 --> 54:08.078
I will.

54:48.451 --> 54:51.079
- Would you like to address the class?
- Of course.

54:51.162 --> 54:54.457
My name is Nobuaki Hida.
I'm a new teacher here.

54:55.041 --> 54:57.460
My mom was a teacher.

54:58.253 --> 55:00.964
I admired her, so I became one too.

55:02.257 --> 55:06.386
I'll try my best to be helpful
to you all as soon as possible.

55:11.516 --> 55:14.602
NOBUAKI HIDA

55:14.686 --> 55:20.483
Hold your wristband to the chosen door
and proceed to the next room.

55:22.319 --> 55:24.154
I need to meet up with Tetsu.

55:46.051 --> 55:47.052
Nobu?

55:48.845 --> 55:51.264
Where are you? Nobu?

55:53.433 --> 55:57.020
- 1 ROOM
NOBUAKI HIDA: 4

55:57.103 --> 55:58.104
Nobu?

56:00.231 --> 56:01.941
I'm here, Sachiko.

56:02.734 --> 56:04.361
Are you all right?

56:06.029 --> 56:08.656
I just went back to B1.

56:09.157 --> 56:11.201
But I got separated from Tetsu.

56:11.993 --> 56:15.747
Did you go to corner room A1?
That might be the exit.

56:16.456 --> 56:18.917
I did, but there wasn't an exit.

56:19.501 --> 56:22.337
We're in C1, right next to you.

56:23.046 --> 56:25.924
We can meet up next turn,
so stay where you are.

56:26.007 --> 56:27.842
- Got it?
- Yeah.

56:31.096 --> 56:33.264
Seventh turn. Begin.

56:46.236 --> 56:47.237
No way.

56:48.738 --> 56:49.739
One each.

56:51.574 --> 56:52.742
We'll be split up.

57:02.085 --> 57:04.838
Usagi, I'm now in D3.

57:04.921 --> 57:06.589
I finally met up with Rei.

57:07.757 --> 57:12.971
If there's no exit in corner room A1,
the remaining corners are A5 and E5.

57:14.097 --> 57:16.057
I bet the exit is in one of them.

57:17.016 --> 57:20.353
Let's look for Sohta and Yuna.
They may know something.

57:20.437 --> 57:21.354
Understood.

57:33.741 --> 57:35.368
Another interview?

57:35.952 --> 57:37.036
Actually…

57:39.205 --> 57:40.748
This is my research.

57:42.375 --> 57:43.668
"Near-death experiences"?

57:45.336 --> 57:47.505
I'm not sure my story helped you.

57:47.589 --> 57:48.506
Don't be silly.

57:51.134 --> 57:53.928
Let me thank you.
Anything you want to eat?

57:55.597 --> 57:56.973
Let me think…

58:12.906 --> 58:13.907
Let's go…

58:16.034 --> 58:17.744
to the world of death together.

58:47.065 --> 58:49.150
Kill her in the next game.

58:49.734 --> 58:51.778
That's your final job.

59:07.877 --> 59:11.381
Your wish will be granted if you kill her.

59:13.216 --> 59:18.680
You'll discover the true world of death
that lies beyond here.

59:24.561 --> 59:25.728
Ryuji, you there?

59:27.438 --> 59:28.356
Ryuji?

59:29.399 --> 59:31.859
- Ryuji!
- Hold your wristband to…

59:31.943 --> 59:32.944
I can hear you.

59:34.153 --> 59:35.363
Let's meet up later.

59:37.031 --> 59:38.700
Let's meet up in B4.

59:43.371 --> 59:46.624
Okay, thank you. Thanks.

01:00:14.861 --> 01:00:17.071
- Nobu!
- I'm so glad to see you!

01:00:17.155 --> 01:00:18.865
- Thank goodness!
- I'm so glad.

01:00:20.241 --> 01:00:24.078
B1 is a minus-one-point room.

01:00:24.162 --> 01:00:25.705
I'll use my points.

01:00:29.417 --> 01:00:31.336
We need to find Tetsu.

01:00:32.420 --> 01:00:34.756
Tetsu?

01:00:35.632 --> 01:00:38.551
Tetsu? Answer me!

01:00:38.635 --> 01:00:39.636
Tetsu?

01:00:40.136 --> 01:00:42.430
Eighth turn. Begin.

01:00:56.194 --> 01:00:57.278
Sohta.

01:00:59.238 --> 01:01:00.948
Wow!

01:01:15.213 --> 01:01:16.089
No.

01:01:28.184 --> 01:01:33.815
Hold your wristband to the chosen door
and proceed to the next room.

01:01:41.864 --> 01:01:42.740
Yuna.

01:01:43.991 --> 01:01:45.118
Sohta!

01:01:49.497 --> 01:01:50.331
Yuna?

01:01:52.250 --> 01:01:53.126
Yuna!

01:01:54.919 --> 01:01:57.672
Sohta. I can't get through!

01:01:57.755 --> 01:01:59.048
Sohta!

01:01:59.132 --> 01:02:00.258
Yuna!

01:02:02.510 --> 01:02:05.930
B4 is a minus-two-point room.

01:02:06.013 --> 01:02:06.848
What?

01:02:06.931 --> 01:02:11.060
2 ROOM

01:02:11.144 --> 01:02:13.813
You now have zero points.

01:02:15.857 --> 01:02:17.108
Game over.

01:03:19.212 --> 01:03:23.424
Sohta?

01:03:31.891 --> 01:03:32.767
Yuna.

01:03:34.393 --> 01:03:36.979
This was a minus-two room.

01:03:39.190 --> 01:03:41.108
What? It can't be.

01:03:43.069 --> 01:03:44.362
No.

01:03:45.279 --> 01:03:46.531
I'm sorry, Yuna.

01:03:50.034 --> 01:03:51.828
I couldn't keep my promise.

01:03:52.662 --> 01:03:55.915
No, Sohta. Open up!

01:03:55.998 --> 01:03:58.084
Someone open this! Please!

01:03:58.960 --> 01:03:59.877
No!

01:04:00.878 --> 01:04:03.631
No! Sohta, don't go!

01:04:03.714 --> 01:04:06.050
No! Don't go!

01:04:06.133 --> 01:04:07.134
No!

01:04:09.846 --> 01:04:10.847
Please!

01:04:24.569 --> 01:04:26.654
Promise me you'll be happy.

01:04:27.154 --> 01:04:29.866
No! Don't go!

01:04:29.949 --> 01:04:32.076
No! Please don't go!

01:04:32.159 --> 01:04:32.994
No!

01:05:30.509 --> 01:05:35.014
YUZUHA ARISU: 9, RYUJI MATSUYAMA: 7
NOBUAKI HIDA: 3, SACHIKO MAKINO: 11

01:05:35.097 --> 01:05:36.223
Sohta has…

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:39.268
Yeah.

01:05:40.519 --> 01:05:42.396
Tetsu isn't here either.

01:05:45.107 --> 01:05:46.108
Tetsu.

01:05:48.235 --> 01:05:49.528
Where are you, Tetsu?

01:05:54.909 --> 01:05:57.161
It's because I left him.

01:05:57.244 --> 01:05:58.329
We don't know

01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:01.374
whether he's dead yet.

01:06:02.291 --> 01:06:04.251
There's just no response.

01:06:08.839 --> 01:06:10.716
B4 is a minus-two room.

01:06:11.968 --> 01:06:12.802
Rei.

01:06:19.100 --> 01:06:23.062
I want you to go south to C5 with Yuna.

01:06:23.980 --> 01:06:27.525
Based on the turn count,
Yuna and her brother passed through E5.

01:06:28.609 --> 01:06:33.447
If E5 wasn't the exit,
then the only corner room left is A5.

01:06:33.948 --> 01:06:34.907
Right.

01:06:35.783 --> 01:06:38.828
I'll join the others in B4
before heading to A5.

01:06:39.996 --> 01:06:43.332
Corner room A5 has to be the exit.

01:06:56.804 --> 01:06:57.847
Yuna.

01:06:59.306 --> 01:07:01.183
Head to the exit with Rei.

01:07:03.936 --> 01:07:06.397
Listen, Yuna.

01:07:07.148 --> 01:07:08.899
Let's go, okay?

01:07:09.567 --> 01:07:10.401
Yuna.

01:07:11.819 --> 01:07:17.742
Hold your wristband to the chosen door
and proceed to the next room.

01:07:18.534 --> 01:07:19.869
Let's go, Yuna.

01:07:42.516 --> 01:07:43.517
Sohta!

01:07:43.601 --> 01:07:45.061
- Yuna!
- Yuna!

01:07:45.144 --> 01:07:47.438
You shouldn't see this! Go with Rei!

01:07:47.521 --> 01:07:48.689
Yuna, come back.

01:07:48.773 --> 01:07:51.233
Hurry! This door will close too!

01:07:51.817 --> 01:07:53.194
Look out!

01:07:56.155 --> 01:08:00.451
The player left in this room
will be forced to stay.

01:08:06.874 --> 01:08:10.252
B4 is a minus-two-point room.

01:08:10.836 --> 01:08:14.423
Please select whose points to use.

01:08:20.679 --> 01:08:22.890
Point deduction confirmed.

01:08:26.894 --> 01:08:27.895
4 ROOM

01:08:27.978 --> 01:08:31.732
B3 is a minus-four-point room.

01:08:31.816 --> 01:08:33.359
Minus four points.

01:08:34.443 --> 01:08:36.112
Let's use mine.

01:08:39.573 --> 01:08:41.992
Point deduction confirmed.

01:08:43.285 --> 01:08:45.579
Tenth turn. Begin.

01:09:07.768 --> 01:09:09.103
No…

01:09:16.527 --> 01:09:19.238
Usagi, how's it going in there?

01:09:20.072 --> 01:09:22.449
Everyone is in room B3 now.

01:09:23.450 --> 01:09:26.996
But our dice roll is forcing us
to split in three directions.

01:09:27.079 --> 01:09:30.749
Plus, one of us will be forced to stay.

01:09:30.833 --> 01:09:33.294
And we still haven't met up with Tetsu.

01:09:34.712 --> 01:09:38.090
Tetsu isn't here in B4 either,
which means…

01:09:41.093 --> 01:09:43.721
Tetsu is in A3.

01:09:45.556 --> 01:09:46.557
Tetsu…

01:09:48.809 --> 01:09:52.354
That room might deduct a lot of points.

01:09:54.732 --> 01:09:56.192
Then what should we do?

01:10:02.281 --> 01:10:04.366
One of you goes
to the high-deduction room.

01:10:04.950 --> 01:10:06.994
The second goes to the minus-two room.

01:10:07.703 --> 01:10:09.622
The third moves away from the exit.

01:10:10.623 --> 01:10:14.335
And the fourth will be forced to stay.

01:10:25.095 --> 01:10:27.348
What the hell, you bitch?!

01:10:27.431 --> 01:10:28.474
Stop it!

01:10:28.557 --> 01:10:29.808
Stop!

01:10:30.517 --> 01:10:31.894
Enough!

01:10:33.062 --> 01:10:34.396
Stop it.

01:10:49.328 --> 01:10:52.373
Let's go to the world of death together.

01:11:26.115 --> 01:11:27.199
Think.

01:11:30.661 --> 01:11:31.745
Come on.

01:11:34.081 --> 01:11:35.332
I gotta think.

01:11:38.794 --> 01:11:39.795
Think.

01:12:15.873 --> 01:12:17.624
EXIT

01:15:05.209 --> 01:15:08.003
Subtitle translation by: Jason Franzman
